Subject: Lands that become creatures for good: animate them at the end of the opponent's turn
Why: AnimateAi.checkPhaseRestrictions lets every Duration$ Permanent animate through at any time,
  so Great Hall of the Biblioplex ({5}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature, permanently; Four-Color
  Control) was animated in the AI's own upkeep (398 times in a 30-games-per-pairing gauntlet of
  Four-Color Control against the meta decks, seed 1, --save-logs), in the opponent's upkeep (123)
  and in its own first main phase (111), and only 12 times in an end step. Mana spent in its own
  upkeep stays tapped for that turn and the opponent's next: on turns 5 and later Four-Color
  Control cast 0.32 spells over the two turns after an upkeep animate, against 1.23 on turns
  without one. Now a land's permanent, instant-speed self-animate with a mana cost waits for the
  opponent's end step, when the mana untaps next anyway.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/four-color-control.txt --vs <the other 17 meta
  decks> -n 100 --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 16-17 Nov 2026, both arms built on
  0001-0011 and 0013 plus a candidate 0012 that was later dropped (it touches only Umbral Collar
  Zealot sacrifices). Without this patch: 42.1% (95% CI 40-44%, 715-985). With it: 53.9%
  (52-56%, 916-784). Difference +11.8 points, 95% CI +8.5 to +15.1 (paired over the same 1,700
  seeds: +9.6 to +14.1; 300 losses became wins, 99 wins became losses). Mirror with the patch
  (`match four-color-control four-color-control -n 200 --seed 1`): 52.0% (45-59%).

diff --git a/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/AnimateAi.java b/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/AnimateAi.java
index 11aeccc6..6c38129a 100644
--- a/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/AnimateAi.java
+++ b/forge-ai/src/main/java/forge/ai/ability/AnimateAi.java
@@ -111,6 +111,14 @@ public class AnimateAi extends SpellAbilityAi {
                 }
             }
         }
+        // A land that turns itself into a creature for good (Great Hall of the Biblioplex) can wait for the end of
+        // the opponent's turn, when the mana would go unused anyway; earlier it leaves the AI tapped out for its own
+        // turn and the opponent's.
+        if ("Permanent".equals(sa.getParam("Duration")) && "Self".equals(sa.getParamOrDefault("Defined", "Self"))
+                && source.isLand() && !source.isCreature() && sa.getPayCosts().hasManaCost()
+                && !isSorcerySpeed(sa, ai) && !sa.hasParam("ActivationPhases")) {
+            return ph.is(PhaseType.END_OF_TURN) && ph.isPlayerNextTurn(ai);
+        }
         // Don't use instant speed animate abilities before AI's COMBAT_BEGIN
         if (!ph.is(PhaseType.COMBAT_BEGIN) && ph.isPlayerTurn(ai) && !isSorcerySpeed(sa, ai)
                 && !sa.hasParam("ActivationPhases") && !"Permanent".equals(sa.getParam("Duration"))) {
